_debt_ebitda":1.3713678188173564,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":58.4,"_gate_accruals":0.049442305562175465,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":5.6,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.19960952831976855,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":57.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0934104426252953,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.017804570822485308,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.298372811081198,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.12665270488925726,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":58.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.04801990023289743,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":49.3,"_gate_pool_share":0.3474626690781566,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0774049169056843,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":63.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.012078611346773755,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":62.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0.005149830861242435,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":5.1,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1084503252610649,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.016923194138285934,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":71.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.10663,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":71.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.429,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":42.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"CECO Environmental Corp. provides critical solutions in industrial air quality, industrial water treatment, and energy transition solutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, China, and internationally. It operates through Engineered Systems and Industrial Process Solutions segments. The company offers emissions management, fluid bed cyclones, thermal acoustics, and separation and filtration solutions; engineering services and environmental systems; and industrial exhaust air contamination treatment and control systems, solutions, and services, as well as intelligent control solutions. It also provides engineered and configured products and solutions, including dampers and diverters, expansion joints, selective catalytic reduction systems, severe-service and industrial cyclones, dust collectors, thermal oxidizers, filtration systems, wet and dry scrubbers, separators and coalescers, water treatment packages, metallic and non-metallic pumps, industrial silencers, and fluid handling equipment, as well as plant engineering services and engineered design build fabrication services. In addition, the company offers solutions for air pollution and contamination control, fluid handling, and process filtration in various applications, such as aluminum beverage can production, automobile production, food and beverage processing, semiconductor fabrication, electronics production, steel and aluminum mill processing, wood manufacturing, desalination, and aquaculture markets, as well as it provides engineered industrial process heating solutions for process industries. It markets its power generation, hydrocarbon processing, water/wastewater treatment, oily water separation and treatment, marine and naval vessels, and midstream oil and gas sectors. CECO Environmental Corp. was founded in 1869 and is headquartered in Addison, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Todd R. Gleason | CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $503K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["CECO Environmental Corp. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.2B market cap on $774M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The company is burning through $5M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 104% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0401057401812688},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $7.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-7678718.26},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Raised 2027 Guidance Will Impact CECO Environmental Stock Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/txse-ceco/ceco-environmental/news/how-raised-2027-guidance-will-impact-ceco-environmental-stoc","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794533067.747,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.426,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"CECO Environmental Corp (CECO) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Orders and Backlog ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ceco-environmental-corp-ceco-q3-190120864.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794510080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"CECO Environmental Corp. $CECO Stock Sold by Lisanti Capital Growth LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/ceco-environmental-corp-ceco-stock-sold-by-lisanti-capital-growth-llc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794484749.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.951,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CECO Environmental (CECO) Stock Sees Fair Value Lift After Higher Analyst Targets","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ceco-environmental-ceco-stock-sees-061125007.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794463885.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What CECO Environmental (CECO) S